# Copy this file to keystore.properties (gitignored, never commit the real
# one) in this same directory, then fill in your actual release keystore's
# details. See RELEASE.md for the one-time signing setup this supports.
#
# storeFile is resolved relative to this module's directory (phone/) unless
# you give an absolute path — point it at the SAME physical .jks file
# wear/keystore.properties uses.
#
# keyAlias MUST be the exact same alias (the same key entry) as wear's
# keystore.properties — see RELEASE.md's "same signature" section for why:
# the Wear Data Layer routes messages by AppKey (package+signature), so a
# phone/watch signature mismatch silently breaks phone<->watch delivery in
# a signed release even though every debug/sideloaded test worked fine
# (both currently happen to share Android's default debug keystore).
storeFile=../release-keystore.jks
storePassword=CHANGE_ME
keyAlias=pipboywatch
keyPassword=CHANGE_ME
